Subject: [PATCH] designate: give each PTR test class its own subnet

The positive and negative PTR test classes each create their own
external network, but BasePtrTest.resource_setup() gives both the same
198.51.100.0/24 subnet and 198.51.100.10-200 allocation pool. Network
isolation does not isolate designate's reverse namespace: designate
derives the PTR zone and record name from the floating IP address, and
_create_or_update_managed_recordset() finds an existing recordset by
(zone, name, type) and replaces its records. The floating IP's UUID and
project are only record metadata.

When neutron hands both classes the same address while both PTRs are
live, the second set reports action UPDATE, so the CREATE assertion in
_set_ptr() fails. The first FIP's record is gone: its status reads
INACTIVE, so its ACTIVE waiter times out after 360 s, and its cleanup
unset returns 404 ("No such FloatingIP"). In the failures observed so
far the colliding pair was test_list_floatingip_ptr_records and
test_show_floatingip_ptr_impersonate_another_project_no_header, with
either test on either side. The failure is intermittent because neutron
picks floating IP addresses at random from the pool.

Reproduced on a 2026.1 cluster with two external networks on
198.51.100.0/24 and two floating IPs forced to the same address: the
second set returned UPDATE, the first read INACTIVE once the second was
unset, and its unset returned 404. The same steps with different
addresses stayed clean.

Give the negative class 203.0.113.0/24 (TEST-NET-3) so the two classes
can never share an address. The CREATE assertion stays: accepting
UPDATE would hide exactly this interference.

--- a/designate_tempest_plugin/tests/api/v2/test_ptrs.py
+++ b/designate_tempest_plugin/tests/api/v2/test_ptrs.py
@@ -57,12 +57,16 @@
             cls.admin_network_client.delete_network,
             cls.external_network['id'])
 
+        # PTRs are keyed by address across external networks. Keep the
+        # positive and negative classes in disjoint reverse namespaces.
+        prefix = cls.ptr_subnet_prefix
+
         # Create subnet for External network
         cls.external_subnet = cls.admin_subnet_client.create_subnet(
             network_id=cls.external_network['id'],
             allocation_pools=[
-                {'start': '198.51.100.10', 'end': '198.51.100.200'}],
-            cidr='198.51.100.0/24', ip_version=4, enable_dhcp=False)
+                {'start': prefix + '.10', 'end': prefix + '.200'}],
+            cidr=prefix + '.0/24', ip_version=4, enable_dhcp=False)
         cls.addClassResourceCleanup(
             test_utils.call_and_ignore_notfound_exc,
             cls.admin_subnet_client.delete_subnet,
@@ -75,6 +79,8 @@
 
 
 class DesignatePtrRecord(BasePtrTest, tempest.test.BaseTestCase):
+
+    ptr_subnet_prefix = '198.51.100'
 
     credentials = ['primary', 'admin']
 
@@ -196,6 +202,8 @@
 
 
 class DesignatePtrRecordNegative(BasePtrTest, tempest.test.BaseTestCase):
+
+    ptr_subnet_prefix = '203.0.113'
 
     credentials = ['primary', 'admin']
 
